    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d391">

                <pb facs="0326" n="317" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg317"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C/1015: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tittmann</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-15T13:00:00+01:00">June 15, 1940—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>91. The Secretary General of the League of Nations has received a joint telegram
                    dated June 12 [<hi rendition="#italic">11</hi>] from President Dodds of
                    Princeton University, Carl TenBroeck, Director of the Rockefeller Institute for
                    Medical Research, and Frank Aydelotte, Director of the Institute of Advanced
                    Study, inviting the Secretary General to transfer the technical sections of the
                    League to Princeton and offering facilities for continuing the work
                        there.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d391-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Avenol is replying direct to this telegram and is declining.<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d391-f2"/> He has asked me to inform the Department of the foregoing
                    and to state that for a number of reasons he feels that he should not accept the
                    invitation under the present circumstances. He added, moreover, that <pb
                        facs="0327" n="318" xml:id="pg318"/> at no time and under no circumstances
                    would he consider such an invitation without prior understanding with our
                    Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tittmann</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
